{
  "body": "Design selects supported outcomes and plausible violations before existing tests; risk guides depth and cost guides realization without waiving required proof. All 24 document models and section-owned parent responsibilities receive coverage accounting; existing Skill, Authoring and Release catalog packages remain the only separate catalogs. Skill adds two independent CI assembly/PR repair procedures; current automation and proposed semantic procedures retain honest classifications. Validation extends existing native identities, result envelope and executor with cross-mode report output and optional duration ranking, worker-time versus wall-time boundaries, full caller-population accounting and safe invocation-owned output. No runner, benchmark service, universal case schema, performance threshold or runtime implementation is added. Independent first-pass finding skill-feature-output-boundary required reconciliation of Skill with Design source-read-only/authorized living-model adoption; author corrected the three current prescriptions without restoring retired methods. Validation also corrects its requirement range summary and an inherited supporting-view link. Delivery must allocate concrete tests/fixtures, missing proof, published-guidance consumers and reporting implementation before final completeness claims.",
  "change_id": "2026-09-17-complete-model-test-coverage",
  "decisions": [
    {
      "actor": {
        "id": "root-design-author",
        "role": "design"
      },
      "id": "complete-model-test-design",
      "rationale": "Preserve all four approved goals through System-owned selection, proportionate coverage for every model, honest realization/fixture gaps, and attributable timing through the existing Validation executor. Design completeness does not establish executable coverage or semantic procedure execution.",
